                },
                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "41669093",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198015229407",
                            "num_reviews": 1,
                            "playtime_forever": 449,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 449,
                            "last_played": 1524607566
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Let me start off by saying this game has a lot of potential.  It is a lot of fun.  Unfortunately there are so many bugs in this game.  The obvious ones are when you play the other two modes, (Infinite and Challenge), there are no graphics/artwork for the objects when placing them on the planet.  \nThe campaign is good and challenging.  You do have to wait a long time for the focus to return to your planet after it changes to the object approaching your planet (i.e., Asteroids, Comets, and other ships).  The graphics weren't obvious enough for me to know what they were without constantly looking down at the items in queue (with the exception of the shields and the mountains). I guess if you play it enough you will get used to it.  The RNG can definitely screw you over in a level.  Had to play a level over and over just because of the RNG.  I dont mind if i mess up, but when i can't defeat a level becuase i am not receiving the proper objects i dont find that fun (this is specifically for the comet levels).  A little bit of balance is necessary.\n\nIf this game was free i would have no problem recommending it including the faults above, but because there is a price i expect a bit more quality.  Hope this helps others.  At the tiem of this review there was only 3 other reviews and they didnt offer too much feed back.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1524604602,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1524604602,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 10,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.6585102677345276,
                        "comment_count": 0,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Hello!\n\nThank you for such detailed review and positive attitude towards our game! \nWe have tested the issue with Infinite and Challenge modes. Graphics/artwork should appear, but at first you need to click on icon of the object in the lower right corner of the screen. So, that building suppose to appear on the planet. If we haven't figured your problem right please describe the issue in more details or simply send us screenshots. We hope that it will help you enjoy the game process.\nWe are working on fixing the problem with game camera and RNG.\nTroubles with receiving the proper objects are solvable. Just play more aggressively – put as many objects as you can, but be careful with mountains – they need some place reserve. This tactic gives results.\nWith best wishes\n\nKeeplanet team",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1526903264,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
